  "name": "astrolog",
  "description": "Astrolog is a multi-platform astronomical calculation engine and chart generation suite designed for high-precision celestial mechanics. It leverages the Swiss Ephemeris and PLACALC libraries to compute planetary positions, house cusps, and aspects across various coordinate systems and house division methods. The system supports terminal-based ASCII output alongside graphical rendering for X11, Windows, and PostScript, integrating global atlas data and IANA time zone information.",
